PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given an array of strings strs, group all the anagrams together. The groups can be returned in any order.
Two strings are anagrams if they contain the same characters with the same frequency.
For example:
"eat" → "aet"
"tea" → "aet"
"ate" → "aet"
Since all become "aet" after sorting, they belong to the same group.
AIM:
To write a Java program that groups all anagrams together using a HashMap.
JAVA CODE:
import java.util.*;
class Solution {
    public List<List<String>> groupAnagrams(String[] strs) {
        Map<String, List<String>> map = new HashMap<>();

        for (String word : strs) {
            char[] characters = word.toCharArray();

            Arrays.sort(characters);

            String key = new String(characters);

            map.putIfAbsent(key, new ArrayList<>());

            map.get(key).add(word);
        }

        return new ArrayList<>(map.values());
    }
}
INPUT:
strs = ["eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"]
OUTPUT:
[["bat"], ["tan", "nat"], ["eat", "tea", "ate"]]
